    "body": "## Line and headline\n\nLine: instruction reconciliation · count 1/3 (this explicit-owner maintenance delivery; no model experiment/reset) · headline M1 37/232 → 37/232; memory20/40 unchanged. M2 saved437/512 + opened0/128 unchanged; unified6/3 retained. Kimi operator line1/3 and historical starling2/3 retained.\n\n## What and why\n\nActive prompts, policy and tracker still permitted CPU learners/dense training matmul and restarted obsolete campaigns after the owner prohibited them. This reconciles them under D25, including the late owner clarification: OP2 Hamilton kernel first → OP1 G2 only → OP3a geometric head → lawful rung0 → OP4/rung0b. G1 is withdrawn, geometric feed-forward blocks are permitted, OP3b remains later research, and the constraint set stays frozen until the first lawful rung0 result except cost/safety. Kimi remains PM; each lab retains its source assignment.\n\nThe operator record now puts source/kernel implementation before integrated training, removes fresh prohibited cuBLAS/CPU comparators and the mixed-unit BPB/nats bar, and defines raw-score/generated-answer measures with numerical replacement bars still pending prospective registration/FIT. **Training and the independent M2 training/rental hold remain; FIT and this delivery release neither.** No partial-trunk fit, automatic fallback, old constructor/SoftSort/bootstrap campaign, hidden normalized-exponential law or renamed dense contraction is authorized.\n\nThe concurrently merged #2258 harness is preserved. Its cache/CPU-work skill are reconciled, and one existing warning test gets a controlled registry fixture so it does not force the historical counter back to an obsolete value. No production harness or Rust/model source changes. Old prompts/status/operator plan remain restorable at aaa210ef4; dated experiments and peer worktrees/jobs/leases stay preserved.\n\n## Result\n\nDecision: KEEP the instruction repair; no model capability result, new acceptance threshold, mechanism retirement or count reset. This is source/policy reconciliation requested by the owner, not TEST FITNESS clearance or model compute.\n\nOwner authorization/claim: [#issuecomment-6135490872](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/2029#issuecomment-6135490872). The [historical operator pre-registration #issuecomment-6134571032](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/2029#issuecomment-6134571032) is amended by D25 and stays held; no FIT clearance is claimed. References identify source history, not compute permission.\n\nExact review head: 8757a97a3689b9cfcacb0d90865c34a2dd45c854. Static policy/hold/device/PM/freeze/order assertions, 60 added relative-link targets, four harness-readable prompts, source-preservation review, claim wording, whitespace and no-softmax ratchet pass. The ratchet remains1649/1649; it is not semantic compliance certification. Existing227-test harness suite PASS locally and in GitHub CI at this exact head (CI22.145s). Harness rules:0 errors; local warnings concern missing historical heartbeat receipts and other labs' retained branches/caps. PR lint:0 errors, one warning because this owner maintenance line is not a model research line. Those observations authorize no peer cleanup or invented count reset. Rust/model tests are inapplicable and NOT_RUN. No build/model/GPU/rental work.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Canonical record: docs/labs/instruction-reconciliation-2026-10-12/README.md\n- [x] New current-state entry with Next; active instructions and stale navigation updated\n- [x] README/STATUS/ROADMAP reconciled; #2028 body prepared for guarded update after protected merge\n- [x] Checks run at this exact head: `git diff origin/main HEAD --check`, `python3 local/validate.py`, `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py`, `python3 scripts/check_no_softmax.py` pass\n- [x] Exact-head harness suite, harness rule check and PR lint receipt posted before queueing\n- [ ] Protected merge, fresh-main commit/source verification, guarded tracker update, owned cleanup and result card\n\nReferences #2028, #2029, #2030, #2032\n\n",
